node_modules/
dist/
python-bundle/
build_cache/
.env
*.log
# Vendored binaries at the repository root (rtk, ripgrep). Anchored: an
# unanchored `tools/` also matched `backend/tools/`, so a new backend package
# would have been silently ignored and never committed.
/tools/
dashboard/.next/
dashboard/node_modules/
bots/auth/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.spec
build/

# ── backend/memory/ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The application's code and this machine's runtime state share one directory,
# and the state must never be committed: it holds the config (with the provider
# keys), the conversations, the memory databases, the logs and the egress trail.
#
# Naming extensions was a losing game. `*.db`, `*.json`, `*.log` and `*.jsonl`
# were listed, so anything else dropped in there — a `.txt`, a `.sqlite`, a
# `.bak` — was committable by `git add -A` and, worse, copied into the installer
# by `extraResources`, which does not read this file at all. So the whole
# directory is ignored and the code is named back in.
#
# `integrations/` used to be an exception, for an empty `calendar_events.json`
# that looked like a seed. It is not: it is the user's calendar, and shipping it
# meant an upgrade installed the developer's empty one over it. The calendar
# loads an absent file as an empty list, so nothing needs to ship.
backend/memory/*
!backend/memory/*.py

# Fetched by scripts/fetch_voice_models.py and bundled on purpose: the offline
# voice needs them present, so this is the one ignored directory that ships.
backend/voice/models/

